# What this test reaches for (format `<path> <name>`). deep-deps mounts each at
# DEEP-DEPS/<name>, and the MOUNT NAMES MATCH THE REPO NAMES on purpose: both
# lints resolve their inputs relative to a tree root, so `DEEP-DEPS/` simply IS
# that root and nothing has to be assembled.
#
# This test used to be handed the whole workspace as $CAOS_PROJECT, so it
# re-keyed on every edit to every file, including edits to other tests. Now it
# re-keys on what it actually reads.
#
# flake.nix is declared although only its EXISTENCE is checked: `keep_rule` in
# lint-flake-src.sh MIRRORS the filter in flake.nix, and the two drifting apart
# is the whole failure mode — declaring it is what makes this test re-run when
# the filter changes rather than when anything changes.
../../rust rust
../../std std
../../flake.nix flake.nix
# NOT for a worktree — this test drives no client. For the TOOLCHAIN: both lints
# use `sed`, which std/bash does not carry (CLAUDE.md), and tests/lib's image is
# the one in this tree that does.
../lib lib
